{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu","id":1001639,"title":"Why is there no Cainite kung fu?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-10T23:03:04-08:00","id":1001639,"title":"Why is there no Cainite kung fu?","content":"<br /> <br /> So the stargazer tribe of werewolves (and presumably any other changer who goes through the trouble to bother) get Kalindo, an art of using transformations between larger and smaller forms to assist in movement and fighting.<br /> Mages of the Akashic brotherhood, the Wu Lung, and other traditions have their own fighting techniques that employ magickal effects (and, since we've all seen one too many kung fu films, aren't that vulgar). With mages, <i>the five point palm exploding heart technique</i> is real.<br /> Kuei Jin use martial arts. They use 'chi' for their powers, so why not?<br /> <br /> And, well, mortals and less powerful splats like changelings could probably learn a few things too. But the point i want to make is:<br /> <br /> Cainites have significantly more strength, speed,stamina and solidness than they should do. Many can generate more strength in an ankle movement than I can with my full leg. If I were to mount one in a submission hold, they could get up on the sheer principle that they can exert themselves without needing to worry about exhaustion.<br /> <br /> Now, Other than a move in a book where with 2 potence or feral claws you could tear a vital chunk out of another cainite to deny blood flow, there's nothing. Which is crazy, because when you pack the power of Haf\u00fe\u00f3r J\u00fal\u00edus Bj\u00f6rnsson into Steve Buscemi, you should expect more interesting results. Your body doesn't change past embrace. <br /> <br /> Now, I know, I know. White wolf have had a problem with racists. Just look at the stats of a Katana in comparison to a good, wholesome European sword. But in seriousness: &quot;Martial Arts&quot; are two words in the english language and Non-Asians have been playing around with fighting arts since at least alcohol and marriage. Be it Greek, Roman, Viking,Turkish wrestling or queensberry rules boxing. From lost American arts to practices hidden during the slave trade, schooled unarmed fighting has existed on every continent. Even Medieval and renaissance Knights had systems to get pesky armoured opponents down for a stab (It wasn't jujitsu) . I can't understate how the idea of advanced unarmed fighting techniques being an exclusively Asian thing is wrong (though I stress that there's nothing wrong with Asian martial arts). And while there's the occasional nice thing in the world of darkness, like a nod in the fianna book about traditional wrestling, the cainites having not developed several different martial arts using disciplines or even basic cainite physiology is just <i>wrong</i>. They're on every continent bar maybe the ones without food. Exposed to every major culture, and they have a variety of clan disciplines that ensure that most'll have their own trick or at least sensibilities.<br /> And now, whilst one could assume elders are strong enough to not need learning to fight proper (they could learn to get up instantly with enhanced strength and speed, or learn how to use a sword without breaking it) You've also got to consider a great factor of cainite learning: Cainites get really bored, early nights weren't filled with things to do, even politicking was limited. They could also practice far more techniques than mortals could without worry for permanent injury and less worry for death. (yep. Frenzy is a factor. But even Brujah could take steps to reduce it's chance to an acceptable risk) The possibilities are significant, and I could probably write a section of a book for them. But yet, we've had very little (point me to the books if I'm mistaken) Not all vampire games are combat focused, and the system sucks for slowness if you've got a few players, but Martial arts could make it more interesting (and potentially more lethal, meaning it's faster.) Vampires have the most potential of any splat for crazy fighting moves, even if they're a grim bunch. Their capabilities allow for more versatility than even Kalindo with comparable gifts (though likely avoiding the territory of a do practitioner, since that's largely for delivering effects) <br /> <br /> This isn't just about fighting. Cainites would just move differently in general if they were trying to exert themselves. They could easily use their mismatched power and powers in dancing or acrobatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-11-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T23:31:47-08:00","id":1001647,"title":"","content":"Basically because no one have written one.<br /> <br /> I am currently feeling inspired, so I have <i>begun</i> writing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:11:00-08:00","id":1001653,"title":"","content":"Myself and my Dark Ages group built up our players' fighting styles based on their country and time of origin, who taught them and how they could adapt that to vampiric powers. Once you get to 5+ brawl rating especially these forms start to disappear though, being replaced by complete flexibility and versatility, beyond what any rote method or single school (or even handful of schools) could ever impart. Thought, experience, skill take you to a level where minimum possible force and movement to succeed starts to become preternatural and alarming.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that, yes, despite conventional wisdom sophisticated martial arts weren't historically exclusive to Sino-Japan and the katana was far, far from the be all and end all of blades. I actually researched a wealth of ancient martial traditions, forging methods and materials etc. for another RPG I'm building and the depth and range of schools, weapon loadouts and styles is immense. With that said I don't put much of that in to V:TM simply because I don't want ST combat to get any slower than it already is. It makes for nice flavour in describing attacks etc. and helps guide choice of specialisations but I don't think the system can stand it going much deeper unless your players are very patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 11-11-2016, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:34:43-08:00","id":1001690,"title":"","content":"In WoD Combat there is a Kindred Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:43:53-08:00","id":1001776,"title":"","content":"Because, with all the book space wasted on blood magic, wonky bloodlines and their powers, we really don't need more space wasted on wargaming mechanics.<br /> <br /> Making Kuei-Jin into kung-fu &quot;take a left through my sword and keep on going&quot; was one of the tragic results of the botched attempt to make vampires more involved with the rest of the splats.<br /> <br /> I like the idea, but 2nd ed Sabbat should have been enough for people to realize that wargaming with VtM was a terrible combination.<br /> They went a long way to fix the past mistakes (except for Kuei-Jin, which are still a problem in crossovers) and made more interesting books (except for the blood magic ones), and DtF had none of that trench coat and katanas shenanigans.<br /> <br /> VtM is a game of survival, intrigue and personal horror with no clear way to achieve any sort of victory, and it should stay that way. I'm not against martial art mechanics, but every effort put into it encourages players to make messes. And every pages wasted on combat mechanics comes at the cost of more interesting and worthwhile material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 11-11-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:24:54-08:00","id":1001908,"title":"","content":"There are hundreds of American and European martial arts, so it is just neglect. The majority of them concentrate on weapons because they were combat focused. The question would be how to represent them.<br /> <br /> If you follow the CoD model, you make a five level Merit. If you follow the cWoD, you charge an additional fifty percent, give a signature maneuver with the first level and additional techniques with each subsequent level. I would suggest allowing one reflexive parry with a specific weapon as the signature maneuver, which would make it quite useful to learn. The techniques would be interesting to develop though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:00:59-08:00","id":1001923,"title":"","content":"Martial arts the ability while highly biased in writeup is simple enough to apply fairly universally across cultures. You have hard styles, soft Styles and weapon styles. There's nothing that says you can't have your Brujah entelench with Martial arts(Soft style) to cover someone trained litterally by a classical Greek wrestler.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want physical abilities that refine the innate powers of the kindred condition those exist. They are called &quot;disciplines&quot; there are even specialized secret techniques for such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:08:16-08:00","id":1001932,"title":"","content":"Cainite Kung Fu: Buy the Martial Arts Ability from one of the supplements that includes it (such as KotE) since it is open to anyone.<br /> <br /> There are extremely few options that only certain supernaturals can get. Even Do is something a vampire could in theory learn (it just requires wholly buying into Akashic philosophy). Kailindo is pretty much it, because it requires WtA shapeshifting to be able to do; and even then a vampire with the right Disciplines, Combo Disciplines, and high enough Generation to burn enough blood in combat to pull things off could then in theory be capable of developing such a style.<br /> <br /> VtM doesn't bother because.... well <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> nailed that. It's not because a vampire can't learn to use Energy Weapons like a Technocrat can; but when is that going to happen? When is a vampire going to end up with a Bane Fetish Klaive with the ability to activate it (not impossible... buy hella rare) to even get to learning how to Klaive Duel? It's that learning such things are such edges cases... it's not worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T15:32:20-08:00","id":1001953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1001690#post1001690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WoD Combat there is a Kindred Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the name &quot;Kibatsumejutsu&quot; and not particularly more effective than just having Brawl. Which is actually true of most martial arts, because unless you're playing a Shih or a crossover with Streetfighter, no one's going to be getting powers via their fighting skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:27:32-08:00","id":1001999,"title":"","content":"WoD Combat did not have that great of a combat system and, quite frankly, purchasing power points with XP never made any sense because it always made more sense to buy up the Ability and just get the power points for free. Anyway, the thing is not to get supernatural powers but, instead, to create a more nuanced combat system that allows you to make more effective characters in combat (which is the point of every combat style).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:35:42-08:00","id":1002054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1001999#post1001999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD Combat did not have that great of a combat system and, quite frankly, purchasing power points with XP never made any sense because it always made more sense to buy up the Ability and just get the power points for free. Anyway, the thing is not to get supernatural powers but, instead, to create a more nuanced combat system that allows you to make more effective characters in combat (which is the point of every combat style).</div> </div> </div> </div>More effective compared to characters that don't have powers to buy, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:24:18-08:00","id":1002105,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts are marginally cheaper than powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T01:47:48-08:00","id":1002157,"title":"","content":"Disciplines and combo techniques are Kindred martial arts. Look at something like Shattered Fog training to turn to mist when hit, that even sounds like a Kungfu Technique. The issue here isn't the lack of martial refinements of the kindred condition. The issue is Do is stupidly broken, its nonsensical even from a mage perspective. It should just be a focus for Akashics nothing more.<br /> <br /> Kalindo was intially created before gifts also covered internal refinments of the Fera condition, now that such gifts exist Kalindo should purely be folded into gifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Narratively though if you want to cover the ground of martial arts, secret techniques training to be your best such is already readily available via Disciplines and Combos a system outside them would be redundant. This is why even KJ which completely fetishes Martial arts doesn't have KJ specific MA as an ability but rather incorporate the fluff of such into various disciplines, the Pranas the SHintais etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T08:15:20-08:00","id":1002223,"title":"","content":"I think that there are Martial Arts Techniques more effective than basic Brawl or Melee that do not require supernatural powers. I do not see the Techniques in KotE, KotEC, or DHX as being anything beyond what particularly skilled mortals could do (though a couple of them require chi manipulation capabilities to use effectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:15:43-08:00","id":1002300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002105#post1002105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts are marginally cheaper than powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And completely unusable to shapeshifters outside of human form, as well as typically being ineffectual against ghosts, the undead or things without a human shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:28:37-08:00","id":1002308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002223#post1002223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there are Martial Arts Techniques more effective than basic Brawl or Melee that do not require supernatural powers. I do not see the Techniques in KotE, KotEC, or DHX as being anything beyond what particularly skilled mortals could do (though a couple of them require chi manipulation capabilities to use effectively).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's room for that, but feel CoD may have done it better with fighting styles vs &quot;Martial arts is a separate skill&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Op was talking about Kindred Kungfu and Disciplines perfectly cover this. And Mortal martial arts as just as available to them as KJ","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:53:27-08:00","id":1002317,"title":"","content":"What I'm saying is that martial arts can develop as a side affect from powers, not that martial arts leads to new powers (though new powers could easily be incorperated) <br /> <br /> Examples<br /> I've learnt to disarm a guy by letting them stab into me, i then twist my body to get the sword out of his hand. <br /> I can climb really easily on account of not getting exhausted. <br /> <br /> <br /> I can try to dodge by recklessly jumping the fuck out of the way with my great strength and i can worry a little less about the landing<br /> My strength is 6. I can hold someone up with one hand as a human shield and an improvised weapon.<br /> My strength is great. I can throw someone up into the air in a single move . They'll land next turn. or I could bat them where i want them<br /> My strength is twice that which my weight should allow. Getting up should be a free action in combat. <br /> I have potence and fortitude. I can use my fingers, now very solid, to poke holes in people and gauge out flesh. All the impact onto a smaller surface area. <br /> I can dislocate joints by squeezing my enemy with just my hand. Use light congratulatory pats to annihilate people. <br /> <br /> I have enought dexterity that I can attempt insane attacks. Like If I get 3 successes on a difficulty 9 strike to the neck, any unsoaked damage kills, paralyses or starts suffocation. <br /> <br /> Odd shit might include<br /> I've fleshcrafted this particular modification...<br /> I've used obfuscate to hide my movements<br /> I've used obtenebration: Shadow play and tenebrous form hides my movements. Arms of the abyss can be used to protect me and pull me out of danger/block for me. <br /> I've used chimestry on this blade so that people dodge badly. <br /> I've made dominate commands as part of a feint<br /> I've used presence to put off my enemies. <br /> Dementation has made my enemy more reckless/conservative <br /> <br /> And for the most part none of this needs new disciplines, not even combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:02:07-08:00","id":1002320,"title":"","content":"Either they are covered by the powers that already exist. Or they are new techniques. Nothing on your list shouldn't be covered by anything other that Discipline Techniques. Ability/Disciplne Combos don't currently exist but would be the reasonable outgrowth here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:26:57-08:00","id":1002357,"title":"","content":"Disarming by being attacked could be a Protean/Fortitude or Vicissitude/Fortitude Combination Discipline. I would say Protean 3 and Fortitude 3 or Vicissitude 3 and Fortitude 3, and I would call it Tar Baby. I would require 1 blood pool and 1 Willpower per turn to use Tar Baby. Each time you are attacked with a melee weapon or unarmed attack, make a reflexive Strength plus Brawl roll. If the number of successes exceeds the successes of the attack, the attack deals no damage and the melee weapon or unarmed attack is stuck. Each turn, a user of a stuck weapon or attack may spend an entire action to get free, though they are required to succeed on a contested roll of Strength plus (Ability) versus your Strength plus Brawl if you choose to spend an action to resist. Any stuck objects are released when you stop maintaining Tar Baby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 11-12-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:09:27-08:00","id":1002376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002357#post1002357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disarming by being attacked could be a Protean/Fortitude or Vicissitude/Fortitude Combination Discipline. I would say Protean 3 and Fortitude 3 or Vicissitude 3 and Fortitude 3, and I would call it Tar Baby. I would require 1 blood pool and 1 Willpower per turn to use Tar Baby. Each time you are attacked with a melee weapon or unarmed attack, make a reflexive Strength plus Brawl roll. If the number of successes exceeds the successes of the attack, the attack deals no damage and the melee weapon or unarmed attack is stuck. Each turn, a user of a stuck weapon or attack may spend an entire action to get free, though they are required to succeed on a contested roll of Strength plus (Ability) versus your Strength plus Brawl if you choose to spend an action to resist. Any stuck objects are released when you stop maintaining Tar Baby.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I'd full on let them do &quot;Taking what is Given&quot; from Boneflowers since its conceptually the same power. So Strength+Brawl difficulty of the Attacker's Pool. with auto soak equal to Fortitude levels. One success captures the blade. Each additional success causes one aggrevated wound as the flesh constricts to destroy the weapon or sever the limb. attacker must gain 3 successes to remove the weapon or limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:35:45-08:00","id":1002398,"title":"","content":"you folk really undersell the no-discipline cainite. you can be obscenely tough just through blood buffing or practice and good blood giving 6+ attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T18:02:26-08:00","id":1002409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002398#post1002398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you folk really undersell the no-discipline cainite. you can be obscenely tough just through blood buffing or practice and good blood giving 6+ attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood buffing is horrifically inefficient. If you want to be a strong vampire picking people up by the neck... Potence is the way to go unless you want to have to eat a whole person every 2 rounds. SImilarly, yes you can heal being stabbed.. but that's blood yo could have spent on something else and unless you are 9th gen or lower its the only thing you can do that round. And if you get hit by somethign that does more than 2 or 3 lethal? it hurts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus.. the concept of refining your supernatural abilities as a kindred is what disciplines ARE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:55:17-08:00","id":1002436,"title":"","content":"Blood buffing is best when it is combined with Disciplines. For example, an 8th generation Kindred can blood buff from Strength 3 to Strength 6, which will last a scene, in a single turn and, when combined with Potence 5, will have an effective Strength of 11 (similar tricks can occur with Dexterity and Celerity or Stamina and Fortitude). Blood buffing can only get you to an Attribute 10, which only lasts for three turns after you stop burning blood, and even that is better if you have the right Disciplines, to give you an effective Attribute of 15.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T07:38:37-08:00","id":1002523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002409#post1002409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Blood buffing is horrifically inefficient. If you want to be a strong vampire picking people up by the neck... Potence is the way to go unless you want to have to eat a whole person every 2 rounds. SImilarly, yes you can heal being stabbed.. but that's blood yo could have spent on something else and unless you are 9th gen or lower its the only thing you can do that round. And if you get hit by somethign that does more than 2 or 3 lethal? it hurts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus.. the concept of refining your supernatural abilities as a kindred is what disciplines ARE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your storyteller's been doing it wrong then. Buffing to max +1 lasts a scene. and buffing past that should last a couple of mins or at least a combat. More than two turns. And another point is that this strength and hardness is irrespective of your physical size. You also can't run out of your breath so no need to conserve energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-13-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T08:17:12-08:00","id":1002534,"title":"","content":"Blood buffing beyond max plus 1 is inefficient. If you assume that the average physical attribute is '3', you can blood buff to '6' without horrible inefficiency, but it is still 30% of a human being per scene. Or you can develop the three physical Disciplines to '3', which gives you the bonus permanently (as well as other goodies), and blood buff to '6 plus 3' in an emergency. Purchasing Disciplines is just more efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:21:16-08:00","id":1002569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002534#post1002534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood buffing beyond max plus 1 is inefficient. If you assume that the average physical attribute is '3', you can blood buff to '6' without horrible inefficiency, but it is still 30% of a human being per scene. Or you can develop the three physical Disciplines to '3', which gives you the bonus permanently (as well as other goodies), and blood buff to '6 plus 3' in an emergency. Purchasing Disciplines is just more efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really depends on your character's age. Most 6th and 5th gens wouldn't care at all about spending that much blood per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T11:22:36-08:00","id":1002571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002523#post1002523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your storyteller's been doing it wrong then. Buffing to max +1 lasts a scene. and buffing past that should last a couple of mins or at least a combat. More than two turns. And another point is that this strength and hardness is irrespective of your physical size. You also can't run out of your breath so no need to conserve energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, 3 turns past your max. SO turn of use(because you wisely reflexively turn it on before you start hitting people), 2 turns then back to six. That's just if you want to keep strength at 8. SInce you also want to be hitting so buffing dex to 8. That's 3 blood next round, Six blood spent at round 2. As an 8th gen that's 3/7s of your blood pool in two rounds. That's enough if you take from one person it will incapacitate and probably kill them.<br /> <br /> Now lets include your plans like &quot;letting people hit you&quot; so now you have to spend blood to heal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But this is still getting off the answer to the subject. The Refinement of Vampiric strength isn't &quot;Blood buff training&quot; its Potence. KIndred Ironbody Technique is Fortitude. There is no conceptual room for a Martial art dedicated to this since the very concept is Disciplines. Now having particular Disciplines grant access to new Manuevers may also be a reasonable position to take but there isn't a place for &quot;Generic Vampire Kungfu&quot; even the game that completely fetishes Martial arts and anime vampires doesn't include the concept, except as I said in Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:30:46-08:00","id":1002603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002308#post1002308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think there's room for that, but feel CoD may have done it better with fighting styles vs &quot;Martial arts is a separate skill&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In short, that's my whole opinion. NWoD/CofD does the martial arts/fighting styles thing just a lot better. WoD favors heavily unarmed and/or Asian MAs (more skills, more manouvers). That's one of the few &quot; '90s-isms&quot; which is truly bothers me. NWoD's Armory books and the whole approach is just simply better, more flexible and covers a lot more, even HEMA.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's just not there in Vamp, because it hasn't any significant role (although I don't agree with the opinion that it doesn't have a valid place in VtM). In Mage it has, because of magickal traditions and paradigms. In WW it also has, because the whole game is more combat focused. Still, I'd be glad if V5 would treat it like CofD and I'd favor the whole backgrounds -&gt;merits approach (and the purcheasable merits after char creation), although I'd keep flaws. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:05:37-08:00","id":1002614,"title":"","content":"Of course, the problem with CoD is that the characters are a lot weaker than they are in WoD. Of course, their enemies are a lot weaker as well, so it balances out, but it is the perception of strength that tends to matter to a lot of players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:35:42-08:00","id":1002627,"title":"","content":"Martial arts can be gained from disciplines. However, disciplines aren't martial arts. <br /> <br /> You shouldn't need a combo discipline to be gauging flesh out with just your fingers. You should just be using brawl differently. Maybe a move might require 'min strength' or something, or 'needs 2 dots of either potence or fortitude' but on the whole, there's nothing that should require a specific discipline, other than maybe clan specific stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:57:22-08:00","id":1002632,"title":"","content":"Well, perceptions may exist, but it's never actually been true (though also never something you can actually just compare because any assumptions on how to compared them risk biasing the results), and it's significantly less the case in CofD 2e (Garou don't get an &quot;autokill mooks with one success on a hit&quot; bonus in Crinos, as just one of many examples). Hell, one of the big complaints about CofD 1e was that alpha-strike Fighting Style users were frequently more dangerous than supernatural combat powers (though both combined and all is worse).<br /> <br /> None of that really matters to the point though, but it isn't about &quot;power level&quot; about about organization of access to maneuvers, and that the CofD give lots of focus to all forms of specialized combat; not just a glut of unarmed stuff and a few hand-to-hand weapons things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T14:16:57-08:00","id":1002636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002614#post1002614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the problem with CoD is that the characters are a lot weaker than they are in WoD. Of course, their enemies are a lot weaker as well, so it balances out, but it is the perception of strength that tends to matter to a lot of players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sooo much less true in 2e CofD. Vampires and werewolves both received substantial buffs in their second edition core books, at least. I haven't read Mage 2e yet so can't comment on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:34:23-08:00","id":1002663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002627#post1002627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts can be gained from disciplines. However, disciplines aren't martial arts.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need a combo discipline to be gauging flesh out with just your fingers. You should just be using brawl differently. Maybe a move might require 'min strength' or something, or 'needs 2 dots of either potence or fortitude' but on the whole, there's nothing that should require a specific discipline, other than maybe clan specific stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Tearing out Flesh with claws? that comes atomatically, you want to cause wierd agg by tearing out flesh and giving people penalties with potence? Ok you're buying an alternative discipline technique. If KJ in all its powergaming fetishization of martial arts wouldn't give you free powers. There's no way you can argue they should exist.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:54:46-08:00","id":1002672,"title":"","content":"It is a mortal martial art technique from KotE Companion (Eagle Claw). For KJ and Kindred, however, Mantis Strike is more frightening because it destroys one point of Chi or Blood on a successful attack, regardless if it deals damage. A group of five mortal martial artists using Mantis Strike could cripple or kill an individual beginning KJ or Kindred within a few turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:08:20-08:00","id":1002682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002663#post1002663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> Tearing out Flesh with claws? that comes atomatically, you want to cause wierd agg by tearing out flesh and giving people penalties with potence? Ok you're buying an alternative discipline technique. If KJ in all its powergaming fetishization of martial arts wouldn't give you free powers. There's no way you can argue they should exist.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to game first, story second, sure. I too look forward to a system where nobody has XP<br /> If you care for story (and XP economy) a little more, then martial arts and disciplines are two related but seperate things.<br /> <br /> You know, In werewolf, There's an example in leaping rake. Be a Glabro or crinos, Or, if you've purchased the gift <i>Hare's leap</i>, you can do it in homid. There's no special purchase for the same move with the gift involved, because people were using common sense when they wrote the power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T22:29:00-07:00","id":1142418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1001639-why-is-there-no-cainite-kung-fu?p=1002627#post1002627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts can be gained from disciplines. However, disciplines aren't martial arts.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need a combo discipline to be gauging flesh out with just your fingers. You should just be using brawl differently. Maybe a move might require 'min strength' or something, or 'needs 2 dots of either potence or fortitude' but on the whole, there's nothing that should require a specific discipline, other than maybe clan specific stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a good ST, you can narrate an effect with the brutal attacks that Kindred can deliver. <br /> There are combat maneuvers in a number of books, always including the heart shot (+3 difficulty Weapon +1 Dam, needing 3 damage after soak, &quot;stakes&quot; vampires, outright kills most other victims) <br /> In the DAV20 book (Because I have it in hand) Bite; Clinch; Disarm; Great Blow; Hold; Riposte; Sweep; Hail of Arrows (letting you break normal multiple action rules)<br /> <br /> Tome of Secrets lets you pick up extra maneuvers for knights due to intense training.<br /> <br /> But in general (IC and OOC) it's more efficient to train your stats and disciplines than having a specialised martial arts action. +1 difficulty for +2 damage after buying a new skill to 3 or 4 and paying for the action as well? Just get a couple of dots in potence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T06:38:42-07:00","id":1142483,"title":"","content":"I would probably just port the mage 20 martial art skill and manoeuvers into a vampire game with a player who wanted to use martial arts. And let them add combo disciplines to give them a supernatural edge<br /> <br /> Most of the manoeuvers seem like they would do just fine representing European martial arts as well as non-European ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}